  "title": "Review: my family",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Last new words: **স্বামী** (*shami*, husband) and **স্ত্রী** (*stri*, wife). In everyday speech many people say **বউ** (*bou*) for 'wife' — it also means 'bride'. (The ব in স্বামী is silent, which you'll learn about in the conjuncts script unit.)\n\nQuick recap of the family map:\n\n| | father's side | mother's side |\n|---|---|---|\n| grandparents | দাদা / দাদি | নানা / নানি |\n| uncle | চাচা, ফুফা | মামা, খালু |\n| aunt | চাচি, ফুফু | মামি, খালা |\n\nAnd remember **ছেলে / মেয়ে** = son / daughter as well as boy / girl.\n\nWhen you hear a word you don't know, ask **X মানে কী?** \"What does X mean?\". **সবাই কেমন আছে?** \"How is everyone?\" is the classic question about someone's family.",
  "vocab": [
